pr_body:
Translate CW text, poll options and media descriptions. Fixes #21247, #22249, #22398, #23676, #24012.

The translation services are modified to accept an array of strings to translate. Both DeepL and LibreTranslate support this.

The translate endpoint returns JSON in a structure similar to the status endpoint (it is a fake example for the purpose of illustration – in practice a poll has no media attachment):
```
{
  "detected_source_language": "de",
  "language": "en",
  "provider": "DeepL.com",
  "spoiler_text": "Spoiler :warning:",
  "content": "<p>Hello :highfive:</p>",
  "poll": {
    "id": "123",
    "options":[
      {
        "title": "Option 1"
      },
      {
        "title": "Option 2"
      }
    ]
  },
  "media_attachments": [
    {
      "id": "110043751121375668",
      "description": "Media description"
    }
  ]
}
```

The result is merged into the Redux state, with both raw and emojified variants (e.g. `spoiler_text` and `spoilerHtml`), just like the original status fields.

Before passing the text to the translation service, custom emojis are rendered to `<img>` elements to prevent the shortcode from being translated. An additional `data-shortcode` attribute is added, and after translation this is used to convert the image back to the shortcode, so I can be emojified client-side. Both translation services leave this attribute intact.

For statuses with a CW the translate button is now visible even when the content is not expanded. This allows the user to translate the CW before pressing _Show more_.
